IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `itepa-types`

-- Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 (UK) — THE THREE GOALS.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2003-1.txt. The formulas in
-- ss 143(3), 182 and 402D(1) are images in the official print and missing
-- from the deposited text; they are taken from the published Act (F1).

§ `Rules`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below nil` a MEANS IF a GREATER THAN 0 THEN a ELSE 0

§§ `Goal 1 — company car (ss 120-144)`

-- s 121(1) steps 1-3, s 132(3): the deduction is "the lesser of (a) the
-- total of the capital sums contributed ... and (b) £5,000".
@ref ss 121(1), 132(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Company car`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interim sum for` c MEANS
    c's `price of the car` PLUS c's `price of accessories` MINUS `the smaller of` (c's `capital contributions to date`) `and` 5000

-- s 139(3)-(4): for 75 g/km or more, "the lesser of (a) 21% plus one
-- percentage point for each 5 grams per kilometre ... by which the CO2
-- emissions figure exceeds 75, and (b) 37%", rounding the figure down to a
-- multiple of 5 (and, by (2)(a), to a whole number). Below 75, the table in
-- s 139(1) is not in the deposited text: NOTHING (F2).
-- s 141(2): a diesel car under s 141 adds 4 points, at most 35%.
@ref ss 139(2)-(4), 141(2)
@export The appropriate percentage for my company car under ss 139 and 141 of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 (UK): for a CO2 emissions figure of 75 g/km or more, 21% plus one point for each whole 5 g/km above 75, at most 37%; for a diesel car to which s 141 applies, 4 points more, at most 35%. NOTHING below 75 g/km, whose table is not in the deposited text. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Company car`  @desc The CO2 emissions figure and whether s 141 applies
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the appropriate percentage for` c MEANS
    IF whole LESS THAN 75
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF c's `a diesel car under s 141`
         THEN JUST (`the smaller of` (base PLUS 4) `and` 35)
         ELSE JUST base
    WHERE
        whole MEANS FLOOR (c's `CO2 emissions figure`)
        fives MEANS FLOOR ((whole MINUS 75) DIVIDED BY 5)
        base MEANS `the smaller of` (21 PLUS fives) `and` 37

-- The tax year runs from 6 April to the following 5 April.
GIVEN c IS A `Company car`
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the tax year for` c MEANS Date 6 4 (c's `tax year beginning in`)

GIVEN c IS A `Company car`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the tax year for` c MEANS Date 5 4 (c's `tax year beginning in` PLUS 1)

-- s 143(2): the days unavailable — before the first day available, after the
-- last, and in periods of 30 days or more.
@ref s 143(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Company car`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days unavailable for` c MEANS
        `not below nil` (Day (c's `first day available`) MINUS Day (`the first day of the tax year for` c))
    PLUS `not below nil` (Day (`the last day of the tax year for` c) MINUS Day (c's `last day available`))
    PLUS c's `days in long periods unavailable`

@ref s 143(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Company car`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in the tax year for` c MEANS
    Day (`the last day of the tax year for` c) MINUS Day (`the first day of the tax year for` c) PLUS 1

-- s 144(1): payments count only if required as a condition of private use
-- and paid "on or before 6 July following that year".
@ref s 144(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Company car`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payments for private use that count for` c MEANS
    IF c's `payment for private use required` AND paidInTime
    THEN c's `amount paid for private use`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        paidInTime MEANS
            CONSIDER c's `paid for private use on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST p  THEN p AT MOST Date 6 7 (c's `tax year beginning in` PLUS 1)

-- s 121(1) steps 6-8; s 143(3): the deduction is (U ÷ Y) × A; s 144(2)-(3):
-- payments reduce the provisional sum, not below nil.
@ref ss 120(1), 121(1), 143, 144
@export The cash equivalent of my company car for the tax year, treated as my earnings under ss 120-144 of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 (UK): the price and accessories less capital contributions (at most £5,000), times the appropriate percentage, less the share for days unavailable, less what I paid for private use by 6 July after the year (not below nil). NOTHING where the appropriate percentage is not available. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Company car`  @desc The tax year, the price, accessories and contributions, the CO2 figure, the days available, and my payments
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the cash equivalent of my car` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `the appropriate percentage for` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST pct THEN
        JUST (`not below nil` (provisional MINUS `the payments for private use that count for` c))
        WHERE
            a MEANS `the interim sum for` c TIMES pct DIVIDED BY 100
            provisional MEANS a MINUS (a TIMES `the days unavailable for` c DIVIDED BY `the days in the tax year for` c)

§§ `Goal 2 — cheap loans (ss 175-182)`

-- s 182: A × I × M ÷ 12, with A the average of the opening and closing
-- amounts, I the official rate and M the whole months outstanding.
@ref s 182
GIVEN l IS A `Cheap loan`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest at the official rate on` l MEANS
    average TIMES (l's `official rate, percent`) DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES (l's `whole months outstanding`) DIVIDED BY 12
    WHERE
        average MEANS (l's `outstanding at the start` PLUS l's `outstanding at the end`) DIVIDED BY 2

-- s 175(2)(b)-(c): less interest than at the official rate, and no
-- exception.
@ref s 175(2)
GIVEN l IS A `Cheap loan`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a taxable cheap loan` l IF
        l's `interest paid for the year` LESS THAN `the interest at the official rate on` l
    AND NOT (l's `an exception applies`)

-- s 180(1)(a), (2): not if "at all times in the year the amount outstanding
-- ... does not exceed £10,000".
@ref s 175(1), (3), 180(1)-(2)
@export The cash equivalent of my cheap or interest-free loan from my employer for the tax year, treated as earnings under ss 175 and 180-182 of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 (UK): the interest at the official rate by the averaging method (the average of the opening and closing balances × the rate × whole months ÷ 12) less the interest I paid; nil if the loans outstanding never exceeded £10,000 in the year, if I paid at least the official interest, or if an exception applies. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN l IS A `Cheap loan`  @desc The balances, the official rate, the months outstanding, the interest paid, the highest aggregate, and any exception
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cash equivalent of my loan` l MEANS
    IF `a taxable cheap loan` l AND l's `highest aggregate outstanding` GREATER THAN 10000
    THEN `the interest at the official rate on` l MINUS l's `interest paid for the year`
    ELSE 0

§§ `Goal 3 — termination payments (ss 402A-404)`

-- s 402E(2): the trigger date is the day notice was given in a notice case,
-- otherwise the last day of the employment.
@ref s 402E(2)-(3)
GIVEN t IS A `Termination case`
GIVETH A DATE
`the trigger date for` t MEANS
    IF t's `a notice case`
    THEN CONSIDER t's `notice given on`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN t's `last day of employment`
         WHEN JUST n  THEN n
    ELSE t's `last day of employment`

-- s 402E(7): "the last day of the period which (a) is equal in length to
-- the minimum notice, and (b) begins at the end of the trigger date" — the
-- trigger date + the notice days, or the corresponding date that many months
-- on (F3).
@ref s 402E(7)
@export The earliest lawful termination date under s 402E(7) of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 (UK): the end of a period equal to the minimum notice beginning at the end of the trigger date (the day notice was given, or else the last day of employment). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Termination case`  @desc Whether a notice case, the notice day, the last day, and the minimum notice
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest lawful termination date for` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t's `minimum notice in whole months`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day` (t's `minimum notice in days`) `days after` (`the trigger date for` t)
    WHEN JUST m  THEN `add months` (`the trigger date for` t) m

-- s 402E(5)-(6): the days from the end of the last day of employment to the
-- earliest lawful termination date; nil if that date is on or before the
-- last day.
@ref s 402E(5)-(6)
GIVEN t IS A `Termination case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in the post-employment notice period for` t MEANS
    `not below nil` (Day (`the earliest lawful termination date for` t) MINUS Day (t's `last day of employment`))

-- s 402D(6): the whole-months case — the period is a whole number of months
-- when the earliest lawful termination date is the corresponding date k
-- months after the last day of employment.
GIVEN last IS A DATE, eltd IS A DATE, k IS A NUMBER, limit IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`whole months from` last `to` eltd `trying` k `up to` limit MEANS
    IF k GREATER THAN limit
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `add months` last k EQUALS eltd
         THEN JUST k
         ELSE `whole months from` last `to` eltd `trying` (k PLUS 1) `up to` limit

-- s 402D(1), (3), (6), (6A): ((BP × D) ÷ P) − T, nil if negative (s 402D(2)).
-- (6): monthly equal pay, notice in whole months, and the period a whole
-- number of months: P is 1 and D is months. (6A): other monthly equal pay:
-- P is 30.42 and D is days. Otherwise P is the days in the last pay period.
@ref s 402D(1)-(6A)
@export My post-employment notice pay under s 402D of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 (UK): basic pay for the last pay period before the trigger date × the days (or months) in the post-employment notice period ÷ the days in that pay period (1 in the whole-months case, 30.42 for other monthly pay), less the other taxable termination amounts T; nil if negative. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Termination case`  @desc The notice, the last day, the minimum notice, basic pay and its period, and T
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my post-employment notice pay for` t MEANS
    `not below nil` (bp TIMES d DIVIDED BY p MINUS t's `T, the other taxable termination amounts`)
    WHERE
        bp MEANS t's `basic pay for the last pay period`
        days MEANS `the days in the post-employment notice period for` t
        wholeMonths MEANS
            CONSIDER t's `minimum notice in whole months`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST m  THEN
                IF t's `paid monthly in equal instalments` AND days GREATER THAN 0
                THEN `whole months from` (t's `last day of employment`) `to` (`the earliest lawful termination date for` t) `trying` 1 `up to` m
                ELSE NOTHING
        d MEANS
            CONSIDER wholeMonths
            WHEN JUST k  THEN k
            WHEN NOTHING THEN days
        p MEANS
            CONSIDER wholeMonths
            WHEN JUST k  THEN 1
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                IF t's `paid monthly in equal instalments`
                THEN 30.42
                ELSE t's `days in the last pay period`

-- s 402C(3)-(4): s 402B applies to the relevant termination awards up to the
-- post-employment notice pay.
@ref ss 402B, 402C(3)-(4)
@export The part of my termination awards taxed in full as earnings under ss 402B-402C of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 (UK): the relevant termination awards (not redundancy pay or the approved contractual part) up to my post-employment notice pay. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Termination case`  @desc The termination facts and awards
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part taxed as earnings under s 402B for` t MEANS
    `the smaller of` (`my post-employment notice pay for` t) `and` (t's `relevant termination awards`)

-- s 403(1), (4): the rest counts as employment income so far as, with
-- earlier amounts, it exceeds £30,000.
@ref ss 402A(3), 403(1), (4), 404(4)
@export The part of my termination package taxed under s 403 of the Income Tax (Earnings and Pensions) Act 2003 (UK): what remains after s 402B (including redundancy pay and the approved contractual part) so far as, with earlier payments counted against it, it exceeds the £30,000 threshold. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Termination case`  @desc The termination facts, awards and earlier payments
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the part taxed above the threshold for` t MEANS
    `not below nil` (rest MINUS `not below nil` (30000 MINUS t's `earlier amounts against the threshold`))
    WHERE
        rest MEANS t's `relevant termination awards` MINUS `the part taxed as earnings under s 402B for` t PLUS t's `redundancy and approved contractual parts`
